 "bloques": [
  {
   "tipo": "explicacion",
   "titulo": "The golden rule: the verb in second place",
   "texto": [
    "In a normal sentence, the conjugated verb always goes in **segunda posición**: **Ich spreche Deutsch** (I speak German).",
    "If you start the phrase with something else, the subject passes behind the verb: **Heute spreche ich Deutsch** (I speak German today).",
    "In questions whether or not, the verb goes **el primero**: **Sprechen Sie Deutsch?**",
    "In questions with question word, the verb remains second: **Wo wohnen Sie?** (where does he live?)."
   ]
  },
  {
   "tipo": "explicacion",
   "titulo": "Verbs that change the vowel",
   "texto": [
    "Some verbs change the vocal with **du** and **er/sie**. **Sprechen** (speak) is one: e → i."
   ]
  },
